          deckDescription: 'One standard 36-card pack derived from the usual French-suited deck by removing the ranks 2, 3, 4, and 5 in every suit. The remaining cards are reused with a special hierarchy of named power cards and sevens that act as automatic tricks in Bräus.',
          suitDescription: 'Four French suits (spades, hearts, diamonds, clubs). Suits matter mainly for identifying special cards such as the Jack of clubs, Eight of spades, King of hearts, and the four sevens, which have unique powers in play.',
          rankDescription: 'Ranks from six up to ace in each suit. Eighteen cards are designated as playable cards in a fixed power order, the four sevens act as trick cards when led, and the remaining high cards form unplayable fillers including the king of clubs as the outcome card.',
          dealPattern: '',
